        "original_id": "7a129653-dd06-5649-a0de-1b74a473c6b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giovanni Furno, Vincenzo Bellini, Saverio Mercadante\n- Roles: composer, music teacher, opera composer\n- Places: Capua, Naples, Catania\n\nFacts:\n- Giovanni Furno was born in Capua on January 1, 1748.\n- Giovanni Furno was an Italian composer and a famous music teacher.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on November 3, 1801.\n- Giovanni Furno taught students including Vincenzo Bellini and Saverio Mercadante.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for his long-flowing melodic lines.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was nicknamed \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Vincenzo Bellini died on September 23, 1835.\n- Giovanni Furno died in Naples on June 20, 1837.",
